{%- comment -%}
  The legal index — the "LEGAL" eyebrow, a rule, and the list of every legal
  page, with the one you are on marked. Design component `OnQM1`, drawn at 280
  wide on all seven policy boards.

  Accepts:
    menu    - a linklist, straight from a `link_list` setting. Preferred, and
              what the section passes, so the merchant picks the menu in the
              editor rather than matching a handle by hand.
    handle  - linklist handle, used only when `menu` is blank. Defaults to
              'legal', which is what a bare render resolves to.
    heading - the eyebrow text. Defaults to 'LEGAL'. Uppercased by CSS, since
              this one is a fixed word rather than merchant copy — unlike
              bf-about-head's label, which arrives already capitalised.
    label   - the landmark name read by screen readers. Defaults to 'Legal'.

  Usage:
    {%- render 'bf-legal-index', menu: section.settings.index_menu -%}

  The consumer loads bf-legal-index.css.

  THE ACTIVE ENTRY IS DERIVED, NEVER STORED, and this is the whole point of the
  snippet. Shopify has no policy template type, so all seven legal pages are
  ordinary Pages sharing ONE template (page.legal) — there is no per-page
  template in which to keep a "this one is active" setting, and a setting would
  be a second source of truth that goes stale the moment a page is renamed or
  the list is reordered. `link.current` is computed by Shopify against the
  request being served, so the marker cannot disagree with the page under it.

  It also survives the AJAX swap for free: bf-page-transition.js fetches the
  real URL from the server, so the index arrives already marked and no script
  has to move a class around to match.

  ONE MENU, EDITED ONCE. Order and membership come from Navigation, so adding an
  eighth policy is a page plus a menu entry with no deploy. The footer's policy
  column should point at this same menu — two lists of the same links are two
  lists that drift.

  Renders nothing at all when the menu is missing or empty. `linklists` hands
  back an empty linklist for an unknown handle rather than nil, so the size test
  covers both.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign handle = handle | default: 'legal'
  assign heading = heading | default: 'LEGAL'
  assign label = label | default: 'Legal'

  if menu == blank
    assign menu = linklists[handle]
  endif
-%}

{%- if menu.links.size > 0 -%}
  <nav class="legal-index" aria-label="{{ label }}">
    <p class="legal-index__label">{{ heading }}</p>
    <hr>

    <ul class="legal-index__list">
      {%- for link in menu.links -%}
        <li class="legal-index__item">
          <a
            class="legal-index__link{% if link.current %} is-active{% endif %}"
            href="{{ link.url }}"
            {% if link.current %}
              aria-current="page"
            {% endif %}
          >
            {{- link.title -}}
          </a>
        </li>
      {%- endfor -%}
    </ul>
  </nav>
{%- endif -%}
